cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project in academic or technical work, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Observability Engineering Framework"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "de Sá Britto Júnior"
    given-names: "Itamar"

abstract: >-
  An open-source observability engineering framework designed for a
  low-cost laboratory environment. The project integrates a Python
  FastAPI application with OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki,
  Tempo, NGINX, k6, and stress-ng to support the collection and
  analysis of metrics, logs, and traces under controlled workload
  and resource-stress scenarios.

keywords:
  - observability
  - OpenTelemetry
  - Prometheus
  - Grafana
  - Loki
  - Tempo
  - FastAPI
  - telemetry
  - site reliability engineering
  - performance testing

license: MIT

